ntdll, win32u, ws2_32, wine.inf: Chromium-based browsers (Edge, Chrome, Electron, CEF) work.
- Chromium renders from a GPU process into the browser process' windows, which macOS does not
  allow across processes (black/white page). Its sandbox needs Windows security features Wine
  lacks, so no renderer starts and every tab stays empty. ntdll adds --in-process-gpu and
  --no-sandbox to the browser process of Chromium-based programs (libcef.dll/chrome_elf.dll
  next to the exe, Electron's icudtl.dat + resources.pak, or msedge/chrome/... exe names), both
  for processes started by other Windows programs and for the first process of a prefix;
  subprocesses (--type=) are left alone. VIRTUAL_CHROMIUM_GPU_PROCESS=1 disables it.
  wine.inf sets the browsers' CommandLineFlagSecurityWarningsEnabled policy to 0, so no
  warning bar about the flag appears.
- ws2_32 implements SIO_ADDRESS_LIST_SORT (order kept as given). Chromium's built-in DNS client
  failed every lookup with WSAEOPNOTSUPP, so no page loaded.
- DefWindowProc's SC_MAXIMIZE shows a hidden top-level window without activating it. Chromium
  maximizes its window in the middle of construction and crashed on the early WM_ACTIVATE
  (BrowserView::OnWidgetActivationChanged on a null keybinding registry); it activates the
  window itself when it shows it.
- Windows that extend their client area into the caption (custom title bars: Chromium's tab
  strip, Electron, Office) keep that area visible below the Mac title bar instead of having it
  cut off: the visible rect always contains the client rect.
- wine.inf maps the Windows CJK font names (MS UI Gothic, SimSun, PMingLiU, Gulim, Meiryo,
  Microsoft YaHei/JhengHei, Malgun Gothic ...) to the Mac's Hiragino Sans, Hiragino Sans GB,
  Heiti TC and Apple SD Gothic Neo, so the default font links of Tahoma & Co. find glyphs and
  Japanese/Chinese/Korean text is no longer drawn as boxes.
